oor as the audited system caller, and settles `sent` + the normalized provider Message-ID or `failed` + `error`/`errorCode` (hint either way). `undoSendMessage` (queued-only, hands `sourceMarkdown` back), `retrySendMessage` (failed-only: job args rebuilt from the row metadata — connector fallback, replyFrom re-resolved, error/undo stamps cleared — immediate, no window), `discardOutboundMessage`, `replyToConversation` (contact-email + connector guards) + `bulkReplyToConversations` (cap 50, sequential partial-failure), `composeEmailConversation` (contact-only, subject required, chosenFrom → `metadata.to`, caps refused BEFORE the conversation exists — the 0.4 atomicity). Routes `POST /:id/reply`, `/compose`, `/bulk/reply` (registered BEFORE `/:id/reply` — Hono's fallback router matches in source order, so the param route would swallow it), `/messages/:messageId/{undo,retry,discard}`. `addJobInTx` now returns the pg-boss job id (stamped as `scheduledSendId` for metadata parity); the undo window is env-tunable (`CONVERSATION_UNDO_SEND_DELAY_MS`, harness 1.5s). Integration: reply → queued (undo stamps + approval completed by the sender) → the delayed job delivers on a fake SMTP (threading + normalized Message-ID asserted), forced failure → `failed`+error → retry re-delivers (retryCount 1), undo returns the draft + the fired job no-ops on the gone row, discard clears a failed bubble, compose opens the outbound conversation, bulk reply 1-of-2 partial failure, send queue drains. inc 56 (Tier B, chat search leg): `domains/conversations/search-chat.ts` twins `search_for_chat.ts` with the same discipline — the Tier-A role gate is nowhere near sufficient, so EVERY row passes the REUSED `conversationAssignmentAllows` predicate (role/team resolved from the caller's identity, never accepted as arguments); the same caps (300-conversation walk, 400-message body pre-pass returning ids only, 25-contact and 50-body match sets) and the same truncation contract (a limit-break is a full answer; a cap-cut names itself); contact matching via the REUSED `rowMatches` + `contactsSearchStrategy`, HTML stripped before body matching. The chat shim's `searchConversationsForChat` honest-empty replaced with the real leg. Integration: subject/body/contact matches for the admin, the member sees exactly their assigned row, a stranger sees nothing. inc 57 (Tier B, address routing): `domains/conversations/routing.ts` twins `address_routing.ts` — the governance hook run INLINE at inbound creation (inside the shim's `createConversationWithMessage`, before downstream notifications observe the row): the org's `conversation_routing` policy FILE (read via `readGovernancePolicyForOrg`; the 0.4 configCache read dies per rule 5) maps the address the customer wrote to (`inboundRecipientAddress`, case-insensitive exact) onto a team queue and/or person; `applyConversationAssignment` validates org membership/team ownership, patches only changed dimensions, audits `assign_conversation` as `system`, and notifies impersonally through the EXISTING collab emitters; an explicit `enabled: false` silences configured rules, and a STALE rule (deleted user/team) warns and leaves the row unassigned — ingest never breaks. Integration: team + person routing (case-insensitive), unknown address, stale rule, kill switch, both bells + both system audit rows. inc 124 closes the row: the scheduled sync packs DO land via provisioning — `seedDefaultAutomationPacks` is the 0.4 `seedDefaultPacks` semantics on the 0.5 store (org-scope packs only, hidden ones skipped, a deliberate deletion's tombstone NOT resurrected, the shipped presentation half refreshed without touching behaviour), and the integration probe watches the real `imap-smtp/sync-emails` pack land at v1 with its trigger and stay at one row on a re-run. The deploy gate stays HUMAN, which is the 0.4 posture: seeding installs the pack, an admin deploys it. The Inbox's own frontend cut over in inc 122                                            